# Damage the frozen paladin's leather armour +3 and SAVE him, so the damage can
# be frozen into tools/fixtures/chars/ (bd inc-vouo). Start from the paladin
# human-paladin-seed4-opt0822.sav, loaded, not generated:
#
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/human-paladin-seed4-opt0822.sav \
#   tools/make_char_fixture.sh human-paladin-damaged-armour-opt0822 \
#       tools/keys/repair-cost-damage-save.keys <seed> \
#       tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat
#
# A wizard-made "minor decay trap" goes on the square to the east and is walked
# onto. The trap picks a random equipped item, so only some seeds hit the
# armour; tools/check_char_fixture.sh and the sheet show which. The first RIGHT
# after the placement is eaten by the "You find a trap" interrupt; the second
# RIGHT opens the confirm prompt.

w
@while "Enter wizard mode" y
@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Create Trap"
"minor decay trap" ENTER
RIGHT
ENTER
RIGHT
RIGHT
y

i
@dump:damaged
ESC

@until "System Menu" ESC
@expect "System Menu"
b                       # [b] Save and Continue; no @quit, so exactly one save
@dump:saved
